record evidence-intake-project.evidence.phase-d-complete/1 : evidence {
    title "97 tests pass, clippy clean under -D warnings, formatting clean. tests/suggest.rs grew to 18, adding duplicate people proposed without merging (both dossiers stay separate), shared forenames and initials left alone, non-person entities never compared, a finding writing nothing and repeating identically on rerun, a finding disappearing once the gap is closed by mapping the proposition to an element, an unsupported proposition reported, the vehicle-stop clock disagreement found naming both sources without instructing which clock to correct, and every analyzer either proposing or reporting but never both. tests/authoring.rs adds two entities sharing a name recorded as two records and a nameless entity refused. Verified by hand: vehicle-stop yields 3 proposals, 1 skip, and 4 findings; authoring `Patel` then running duplicate-entity proposes possibly_same_person against the fixture's `Jordan Patel` and it appears in the review queue naming the analyzer."
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:680ae34e620880df090096477a2ac1a3637fea55
    command "cargo fmt --check && cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings && cargo test --all-features"
    summary """
        97 tests pass, clippy clean under -D warnings, formatting clean. tests/suggest.rs grew to 18, adding duplicate people proposed without merging (both dossiers stay separate), shared forenames and initials left alone, non-person entities never compared, a finding writing nothing and repeating identically on rerun, a finding disappearing once the gap is closed by mapping the proposition to an element, an unsupported proposition reported, the vehicle-stop clock disagreement found naming both sources without instructing which clock to correct, and every analyzer either proposing or reporting but never both. tests/authoring.rs adds two entities sharing a name recorded as two records and a nameless entity refused. Verified by hand: vehicle-stop yields 3 proposals, 1 skip, and 4 findings; authoring `Patel` then running duplicate-entity proposes possibly_same_person against the fixture's `Jordan Patel` and it appears in the review queue naming the analyzer.
